    {
      "text": "And I knew it was the groan of mortal terror. It was not a groan of pain or of grief. Oh no, it was the lowest-difold sound that arises from the bottom of the soul when overcharged with aw. I knew the sound well. Many a night, just at midnight when all the world slept. It has wellled up in my own bosom. Deepening.",
